      say: `Now the fixtures tell their stories. One credential copies the sample's trailing slash and gets the environment's letter case wrong, so it fails three ways, including the exchange. Another copies the template's stray space in the audience. A credential someone added in the portal shows up as a warning. One conversion has run forty clean days with the owner's approval, so it's the single disable in the plan, while another's old secret was still signing in weeks after cutover. Then you dry-run with the approved hash, apply to the fake in order, and watch a hash nobody approved get refused.`,
      detail: `Step 4, read the findings: Get-Content out/federation/findings.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json | Format-Table Rule, Severity, ObjectKey: NPI-WIF-03, NPI-WIF-02 and NPI-WIF-08 Finding on conv-02/payroll-prod; NPI-WIF-07 Warn on conv-02/payroll-test; NPI-WIF-04 and NPI-WIF-08 Finding on conv-03/github-intranet-tag; NPI-WIF-01 Finding on conv-06; NPI-WIF-09 Finding on conv-08. payroll-prod copies the Azure PowerShell sample's issuer, with its trailing slash, and names the environment Production where the workflow's is production: two findings, and an exchange test that fails. payroll-test was added in the portal and isn't in the file. github-intranet-tag copies the ARM template's audience, leading space and all. conv-06 gives an Azure Functions app a certificate when a managed identity is available. conv-08's secret still signed in on October 28, eight weeks after cutover. Step 5, read the exchange tests (Credential, SubjectSource, Passed): payroll-prod derived False; github-main derived True; github-intranet derived True; github-intranet-tag derived False; aks-webfront derived True; gh-reports derived True. aks-webfront is on an identity the plan will create: its test ran against a client ID marked pending:, and its real exchange waits for Lab 2. Step 6, read the conversions: conv-01 managedIdentity Ready ReadyToDisableLegacy day 40; conv-02 federatedCredential Blocked AwaitingCutover; conv-03 federatedCredential Blocked AwaitingCutover; conv-04 managedIdentity NotReady AwaitingCutover; conv-05 certificate NotReady AwaitingCutover; conv-06 certificate Blocked AwaitingCutover; conv-07 managedIdentity Ready ParallelRunning day 15; conv-08 federatedCredential Ready LegacyStillInUse day 59. conv-01 (svc-hrsync to the user-assigned identity id-hrsync) has run 40 days with the identity signing in and no logon by the old account since cutover, and its owner approved: the one disable in the plan. conv-07's window ends November 14. conv-03 is blocked by its tag credential, though github-intranet itself is created. conv-05, an on-premises task with no OIDC issuer, goes to a certificate under Chapter 04. Step 7, dry-run the plan with its approved hash: $sha = (Get-FileHash out/federation/plan.json -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLower(), then ./Invoke-NpiFederation.ps1 -Cloud gcc -PlanPath out/federation/plan.json -ApprovedSha256 $sha -FixturePath tests/fixtures/ch05/tenant.json -OutputPath out/federation-dryrun gives "DryRun: 4 WouldSend": DisableLegacy, Disable-ADAccount -Identity ad000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001; CreateCredential, POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/applications/0a000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004/federatedIdentityCredentials; CreateIdentity, PUT .../userAssignedIdentities/id-webfront?api-version=2024-11-30 on management.azure.com; CreateCredential, PUT .../userAssignedIdentities/id-webfront/federatedIdentityCredentials/aks-webfront?api-version=2024-11-30. Step 8, apply it to the fake with -Apply, then try a hash nobody approved (-ApprovedSha256 ('0' * 64)): "Apply: 4 Sent", in the same order, the identity before its credential; then the refusal, "The plan's SHA-256 is 5ec0a52c…, not the approved 0000…; refusing to run a plan nobody reviewed." Step 9, Invoke-Pester -Path tests. Expected result: 513 tests passing across the example, out/federation/manifest.json listing 20 reads (5 application reads, 4 credential lists, 1 service principal, 4 sign-in pages, 2 identities, 2 role assignment reads, 2 AD reads) and 6 token exchange tests sent to the fake, and out/federation-apply/manifest.json listing the prechecks and the four writes. Delete out when you're done. The chapter's own tests: 17 in tests/NpiFederationSamples.Tests.ps1 (Microsoft's samples, run as published) and 38 in tests/NpiFederation.Tests.ps1 (the call list and its least-privilege check, the client and the token exchange harness, the claims and credential checks, the order, each finding and plan action, the 20-credential limit, the deterministic plan hash, each parallel run status, the writer's refusals, dry run, -Apply in order, the prechecks that skip, and the entry script and its manifest).`,
